SYNTHETIC FIXTURE (issue #321 C-sweep) — NOT a real benchmark.
Hand-authored coordinator "Received event:" lines with ROUND prove_ms values
chosen purely so the THROUGHPUT math (leaf_cpu / fold_cpu / total / core-sec-per-
block / cold-vs-warm fold CPU / fleet-sizing projection) has clean, checkable
assertions in test_extract_throughput.py. Every number is invented for test
determinism and MUST NEVER be copied into reports/ or treated as measured.

Design (blocks defaults to 1, single-block run):
  leaves prove_ms: 1000 + 2000 + 3000 + 6000 = 12000 ms => 12.0 core-sec
  folds  prove_ms: 3000 (cold) + 4000 (warm) + 1000 (warm) = 8000 ms => 8.0 core-sec
  total = 20.0 core-sec ; blocks=1 => core_sec_per_block = 20.0
  cold fold (is_first_task_on_pod=true): 3000 => 3.0 core-sec
  warm fold (is_first_task_on_pod=false): 4000 + 1000 = 5000 => 5.0 core-sec
  fleet @10bps: cores = 20.0*10 = 200 => ceil(200/60) = 4 c3d nodes
  fleet @12bps: cores = 20.0*12 = 240 => ceil(240/60) = 4 c3d nodes
